comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-27T21:13:39.907Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status pm search for 2026-09 dependency refresh and Sentry 11/Vitest 5/TypeScript 7 found historical closed refresh items, none covering the September 27 available versions. Open/in-progress lists contained no active dependency refresh."
  "2026-09-27T21:21:58.487Z","harness:codex","Live dependency census after compatible refresh: @types/node 26.6.3, greptile 3.6.0, jscpd 5.3.2, knip 6.38.0, and marked 18.0.14 are installed and locked. pnpm audit reports no known vulnerabilities. Major upgrades remain canonical: pm-fokyhh (Vitest 5 excluded by CodSpeed peer ^3.2 || ^4), pm-do5b (TypeScript 7 excluded by typescript-eslint peer <6.1 and compiler API migration), pm-ksr40d (npm-package-arg 14 requires Node 22.22.2 versus published >=22.18.0), and pm-t3jxjj (Sentry 11 published September 23, below seven-day adoption window). Registry metadata was verified live September 27. No peer or engine override was applied."
  "2026-09-27T23:32:26.192Z","harness:codex","Verification: compatible package refresh passed pnpm audit (all and production), supply-chain cooldown, typecheck, 9380-test exact full coverage 100/100/100/100, packed npm/npx/bunx smoke, and the linked full repository static gate in an isolated 2824-item tracker snapshot. An initial linked static run used the default empty schema tracker and failed repository assurance; its test link was corrected to tracker context and the complete gate then passed. Four incompatible major upgrades remain separately governed as open work."
